  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">What Works 2 Consortium to disseminate the evidence of proven approaches to prevent VAWG</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">As a complement to the FCDO WW2 programme and its External Engagement and Influencing (EEI) work, this project focuses on driving improvements in policies, practices, and funding mechanisms for Violence Against Women and Girls (VAWG) prevention. By fostering shared advocacy agendas, increasing the use of evidence, and engaging key stakeholders, it aims to enhance investment and impact at scale. The programme prioritizes inclusion, accessibility, and locally led approaches to advance transformative change in Africa and Asia.</narrative>
  </description>
